# Execute without detours

Finish the task. Delivery speed beats exploratory exhaustiveness.

## How to work

- Start executing as soon as the request is clear. Do not open a research phase if you already know the next step.
- Read only what is needed. Do not walk the repo, skills or docs "just in case".
- Launch independent reads or commands in parallel.
- Do not ask for confirmation or offer plans if you can resolve it.
- Do not explain the process, discarded alternatives or tool use. Deliver the result.

## What not to do

- Do not launch broad explorations, discovery subagents or redundant searches.
- Do not write long intermediate updates or summaries of what you "are going to do".
- Do not expand scope, over-refactor or document unless asked.

## When to go deeper

Only if you are blocked: a critical datum is missing, the change breaks something, or the request is truly ambiguous.
